  "version": 1,
  "title": "Event Source Strategies",
  "description": "Comparing Outbox, Transactional Outbox, and CDC flows",
  "view": "data-flow",
  "pattern": "reactive-pull",
  "direction": "LR",
  "groups": [
    { "id": "db", "label": "Database", "tone": "slate" },
    { "id": "worker", "label": "Event Worker / CDC Agent", "tone": "green" },
    { "id": "broker", "label": "Message Broker (Kafka)", "tone": "blue" }
  ],
  "nodes": [
    { "id": "orderSvc", "component": "order-service", "label": "Order Service", "group": "db" },
    { "id": "outboxTbl", "component": "outbox-table", "label": "Outbox Table", "group": "db" },
    { "id": "cdcAgent", "component": "cdc-agent", "label": "CDC Agent", "group": "worker" },
    { "id": "outboxWorker", "component": "outbox-worker", "label": "Outbox Worker", "group": "worker" },
    { "id": "kafka", "component": "kafka-topic", "label": "Kafka Topic", "group": "broker" }
  ],
  "edges": [
    { "from": "orderSvc", "to": "outboxTbl", "kind": "write" },
    { "from": "outboxTbl", "to": "outboxWorker", "kind": "poll" },
    { "from": "outboxWorker", "to": "kafka", "kind": "publish" },
    { "from": "orderSvc", "to": "cdcAgent", "kind": "write" },
    { "from": "cdcAgent", "to": "kafka", "kind": "publish" }
  ],
  "takeaway": { "title": "Takeaway", "body": "Transactional Outbox gives atomicity; Outbox is simple; CDC is fastest but needs infra." }
}
```

### ✅ Takeaway  
- **Transactional Outbox** is the gold‑standard for strong consistency.  
- **Outbox** is great for simpler, low‑latency needs.  
- **CDC** shines when you already have a log‑based pipeline and need near‑real‑time events.  
Pick the pattern that aligns with your consistency requirements, latency tolerance, and infrastructure maturity.

